---
import GuidePage from '../../layouts/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="Moving to London: Your Checklist"
  description="A practical, week-by-week checklist for moving to London — from before you arrive to your first three months. Everything in one place, in the right order."
  category="The Anchor"
  categoryHref="/anchor"
  heroBg="var(--terracotta-pale)"
  readTime="5 min"
  lastUpdated="May 2026"
>

  <p>
    Moving to a new country involves a hundred small tasks that nobody hands you in a list.
    So here's the list. Work through it at your own pace — not everything will apply to
    everyone, and the order may shift depending on your situation. But this covers the
    essentials.
  </p>

  <!-- ── Before you arrive ─────────────── -->
  <h2>Before you leave home</h2>

  <div class="checklist-group">
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Sort your visa</strong>
        <p>Make sure your visa is approved and you understand the conditions — what you can and can't do, and when it expires. See our <a href="/anchor/visas">Visas guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Arrange temporary accommodation</strong>
        <p>Book a short-term let, Airbnb, or stay with a friend for your first 2–4 weeks. Don't rush into a permanent tenancy from abroad.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Open a Wise account</strong>
        <p>You can get UK bank details before you arrive, which is useful if your employer needs an account number on day one. See our <a href="/anchor/banking">Banking guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Scan and back up all documents</strong>
        <p>Passport, visa, academic certificates, driving licence, birth certificate, insurance documents. Store in cloud storage AND email yourself copies.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Check what you can bring into the UK</strong>
        <p>There are restrictions on food, plants and some goods — especially post-Brexit. Check <a href="https://www.gov.uk/bring-pet-to-great-britain" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gov.uk</a> if you're bringing a pet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Arrange international health cover for the journey</strong>
        <p>Travel insurance for the move itself. Your IHS gives you NHS access once you arrive, but not during travel.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Tell your home bank you're moving</strong>
        <p>So your cards don't get blocked when you land. Also check their international fees.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Day 1 ───────────────────────────── -->
  <h2>Day one in London</h2>

  <div class="checklist-group">
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Buy a UK SIM card</strong>
        <p>You need a UK number to open a digital bank account. Giffgaff, Three and iD Mobile all do no-contract pay-as-you-go SIMs — most are available at airports, supermarkets and corner shops.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Open a Monzo or Starling account</strong>
        <p>Do this on your first day. No proof of address needed, takes 10 minutes. See our <a href="/anchor/banking">Banking guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Set up transport</strong>
        <p>Get an Oyster card from any Tube station, or just use a contactless debit card — they charge the same daily capped rate. Download <strong>Citymapper</strong> for navigation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Download useful apps</strong>
        <p>Citymapper (transport), TfL Go (Tube status), Deliveroo or Uber Eats, NHS app, Rightmove or SpareRoom (flat hunting), WhatsApp (most people in London use it).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Week 1 ──────────────────────────── -->
  <h2>Your first week</h2>

  <div class="checklist-group">
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Collect your Biometric Residence Permit (BRP)</strong>
        <p>Must be collected from the Post Office named in your visa within 10 days of arriving. Do not miss this window.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Register with a GP</strong>
        <p>Find your nearest surgery accepting new patients at <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/service-search/find-a-gp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nhs.uk</a> and register as soon as you have an address. See our <a href="/anchor/healthcare">Healthcare guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Start flat hunting</strong>
        <p>Use Rightmove, Zoopla, SpareRoom or OpenRent. View in person where possible. See our <a href="/anchor/renting">Renting guide</a> for what to look out for.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Complete Right to Work check if starting a job</strong>
        <p>Your employer must verify your right to work before your first day. Bring your passport and BRP/visa.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Apply for a National Insurance number</strong>
        <p>You'll need this to work and pay tax. Apply online at <a href="https://www.gov.uk/apply-national-insurance-number" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gov.uk</a>. You can start work before it arrives if your employer has your other documents.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Register with a dentist</strong>
        <p>Waiting lists are long. Register at an NHS dentist early even if you don't need treatment — find one at <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/service-search/find-a-dentist" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nhs.uk</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Month 1 ─────────────────────────── -->
  <h2>Your first month</h2>

  <div class="checklist-group">
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Register on the electoral roll</strong>
        <p>Even if you're not sure you can vote, registering significantly helps your UK credit score. Do it at <a href="https://www.gov.uk/register-to-vote" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gov.uk/register-to-vote</a> once you have a permanent address.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Sort council tax</strong>
        <p>Once you have a permanent address, you're responsible for council tax (unless a full-time student). Contact your local council to register. Single-person households get a 25% discount.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Get contents insurance</strong>
        <p>Your landlord's insurance does not cover your belongings. Contents insurance is usually inexpensive and worth having. Compare quotes on MoneySupermarket or GoCompare.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Set up UK utilities and broadband</strong>
        <p>If not included in your rent: energy (Octopus Energy is well-rated), broadband (compare via Uswitch), and water (Thames Water — you can't switch provider).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Open a traditional bank account</strong>
        <p>Once you have a proof of address, consider opening an account with a high street bank for longer-term financial stability. See our <a href="/anchor/banking">Banking guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Start building your UK credit history</strong>
        <p>Being on the electoral roll, paying bills on time and using a credit-builder card all help. Your score starts at zero — it takes time, but start early.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Ongoing ─────────────────────────── -->
  <h2>First three months and beyond</h2>

  <div class="checklist-group">
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Exchange your driving licence</strong>
        <p>If you hold a licence from certain countries, you can exchange it for a UK licence without taking a test — but you must do this within 12 months of becoming resident. Check eligibility at <a href="https://www.gov.uk/exchange-foreign-driving-licence" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gov.uk</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Sort your pension</strong>
        <p>If you're employed, your employer must automatically enrol you in a workplace pension (under auto-enrolment rules). Check you're enrolled and consider increasing your contributions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Self-assessment tax return (if self-employed)</strong>
        <p>If you have any self-employed income, register with HMRC and submit a Self Assessment return. Deadline is 31 January each year for the previous tax year. Register at <a href="https://www.gov.uk/log-in-file-self-assessment-tax-return" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gov.uk</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Note your visa expiry date</strong>
        <p>Set a reminder at least 3–4 months before it expires. If you want to stay, start your extension application early. Don't let it lapse. See our <a href="/anchor/visas">Visas guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-item">
      <span class="ci-marker" aria-hidden="true">○</span>
      <div class="ci-body">
        <strong>Find your people</strong>
        <p>This one matters. London is huge and can be lonely at first. Events, language exchanges, meetups — see <a href="/connector">The Connector</a> for ways to build your community here.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</GuidePage>

<style>
  /* Checklist-specific styling */
  .checklist-group {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    margin-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-10);
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(61, 90, 64, 0.1);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .checklist-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-6);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(61, 90, 64, 0.07);
    background: var(--white);
    transition: background 0.18s ease;
  }

  .checklist-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .checklist-item:hover {
    background: var(--cream);
  }

  .ci-marker {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--terracotta);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .ci-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .ci-body strong {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--text-dark);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .ci-body p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-medium);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
